# Checkout on the windows-latest runner defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which turns every shell
# script into CRLF and breaks `scripts/*.sh` under Git Bash ("$'\r': command not found"), shifts
# line-based golden files and makes `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` differ. Keep LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jar binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.so binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# Gradle wrapper (android/): the shell script must stay LF, the batch file is CRLF, the jar is a committed binary
# whose SHA-256 is checked against Gradle's published checksums (docs/supply-chain.md).
android/gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
